  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 315 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nThe active pattern persist into Wednesday and Thursday, as northwest \nflow continues aloft. This will keep a near daily threat for showers \nand thunderstorms across the area, as storms initiate and move east \noff the high terrain. It will also keep the area from seeing \ndangerous heat indicies through the end of the workweek, with daily \nhighs remaining in the lower 90s. That said, conditions are expected \nto remain humid and could push heat index values into the middle \n90s by Thursday. Stronger upper high pressure then begins to \nestablish across the Four Corners as we head into this weekend, with \nflow weakening aloft and becoming more northerly. Heights rise aloft \nand this looks to bring drier conditions back to the area for Friday \nand into the weekend. Persistent warm advection will also boost \nhighs back towards the middle 90s by early next week, with NBM \nprobabilities creeping upwards (~50-70% probability of MaxT >95F) \nfor much of the area. This could bring a return of heat concerns as \nwe head into August, and trends will continue to be monitored.",
